The laser resolves against an asteroid pool where a hit can mutate the current
record into one child and activate another formerly free slot. Iterating the
live pool directly would therefore let a single beam recursively hit children
that did not exist when it fired.

Capture the 32-slot active set in an `i32` bit mask before collision resolution,
then visit only those recorded indices. Still verify that each recorded slot is
active before hitting it, because an earlier effect may legitimately retire it.
The WAST control uses one large beam-aligned asteroid plus one unrelated active
asteroid and requires three survivors after the split: both new children and the
unrelated rock.
